NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1065,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,4,3,2,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":2.9387,"rank":0.0523,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV001201","role":"target","render":{"description":"Predictions that a sick man will recover, will plough first with a white horse and later with a black horse, and that the black horse will pull the hearse, come true. The horses first harnessed to the hearse refuse, so the black horse has to be harnessed.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43204","original":"Voorloop. \nSchoenmaker vertelt.\n\nOal Kamies noast ons was de haile winter al aon 't sukkeln.\n't Gung dan veur-, dan achteroet,\nBuurman Wessels was 't er op 'n dag hèn west te kieken, hou d' oale 't muik.\n\"Kamies gait achteroet, hai hoal 't nich meer,\" zee hai.\nMoar opa, oal Steffen, zee.\n\"Nee Wessels, Kamies wordt weer beter.\nHai hef nou 'n wit peerd. En 't volgend veurjoar plougt hai 't land mit 'n zwaarde. \nDat zwaarde peerd brengt hum vot.\" \n't Widde wör verkoft en 'n zwaarde kwam d'r veur in de ploats.\nEen buurman hef hiermit de grond pluigd.\nVolgende zömmer störf Kamies.\nVeur de woagen zol 'n peerd van de buren.\nKamies zien aigen har er nog nooit veur west en doarum wol ze hom laiver nich broeken. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV000905","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Before there is a road, the sound of a dog cart and the barking of dogs is heard.","place":"Ter Apel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43087","original":"Maar wel is het waar, dat veel mensen in het veen een hondekar hebben horen ratelen. Ook hoorden ze de hond blaffen.\nLang voor er een weg was en voor er later inderdaad een hondekar langs trok.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.87667,7.05972]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006906","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that one day many soldiers would come with wagons without horses. When the Canadians arrive in 1945, someone remembers this.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43580","original":"Veurloop.\nt Is n hail zet leden. Oabram zee es n moal: “Hier koomt nog ais n haile bult seldoatn. Ik zai ze bie t hoes van H. en bie K en op t haim van Z. Zai hebt woagens bie zuk zunder peerden.\n Toun in 1945 de Canadezen kwamen, was dr nog aine oale, dei zuk dat vertelsel van de spoukkieker in t zin schoot. Hai lag op berre en kun nait best wat zegn, omdat e verlamd was. \nMoar zoveul begreepn wie wel van zien “hoi, hoi”, dat e zegn wol:“Oabram zee t ja al?”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV008709","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Noise in the horse stable in the evening is an omen that a horse will kick something to pieces.","place":"Wessinghuizen","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45305","original":"t Gebeurde wol is, dat ze s oavends wat in t peerdstaal heurden. Kiekn deden ze maistied nich, man ze wuzzen wol, dat t peerd gauw wat stukn hou-en zol; door was t n veurbeduudsel van.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.0525,7.075]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessinghuizen.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3058,"rank":0.6075,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2266","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"You were warned not to walk in the cart track or on the bridle path at night. Because there you could meet evil spirits.","place":"Heesselt","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127631","original":"Dat weet ik ook nog. Je werd gewaarschuwd om 's nachts niet in 't wagenspoor of in 't paardenpad te lopen. Want daar kon je de boze geesten tegenkomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Heesselt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1037,"rank":0.1339,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ083803","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Someone predicts that a relative will die six weeks later. The prediction is exactly right.","place":"Eastermar","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32807","original":"Yn 'e famylje fan myn wiif to Burgumerheide wie ien tige min. De famylje kom delsetten. (Mar hy is wer better woarn).\nDoe sei ien fan 'e famyljeleden: \"Mei seis wiken binne wy wer byinoar.\"\nOp 'e kop om't ôf, krekt seis wiken letter stoar der in broer fan skoanheit. Dat wie Sjouke Dykstra.\nDyselde hie 't dus wol goed sjoen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ103103","role":"omen","render":{"description":"The same fellow once predicted a fire, which happened six weeks later when lightning struck.","place":"Jistrum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37196","original":"Mei dyselde maet wie ik to Kûkherne op in plaets fan 'e Veenlands. Der wenne in boer op, dat wie in Hoekstra. Dy hie in soan: Bouwe Hoekstra.\nMyn maet sei tsjin Bouwe: \"Dizze plaets brânt skielk ôf.\"\nSeis wiken letter gebeurde it. De wjerljocht sloech yn. Myn maet hie him fan tofoaren al yn 'e brân sjoen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1276","role":"omen","render":{"description":"If someone had died on Friday or Saturday, they were not buried. If that corpse was still above ground on Sunday, someone else in the village would die within six weeks.","place":"Well","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72785","original":"En daar nog iets over dan. As nou een vroue of een man of een kend vrijdags of zaoterdags gesturve was, dan wier 't niet begrave. Ston da lijk bove aarde op zondag, dan kreeg de hier op 't dorp binne zes weke weer unne dode.","lang":"Gelderland dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","6 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":6},"on_success":{"chime":6,"digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.7442,"rank":0.8621,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BOEKV094","role":"top","render":{"description":"A father and son live in a hole under the ground. To rob and murder passers-by, they stretch a rope with a bell across the road so they can hear passers-by. One day a girl comes by.","place":"Amen","prov":"Dr.","year":1890,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"G.J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/34975","half":"top"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST041","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They are badly frightened because they think it is the ill-omened figure of a wit wief (white lady). Later they see that the figure is not a wit wief but a white goat standing with its legs against the tree, eating the leaves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0237","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"If you enter this orchard at night, you may meet a white woman riding a pig. Because this woman haunts the place, the farmer cannot find any staff.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST291","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Still, he returns with a bag full of gold. He marries the daughter of a rich farmer. Because the farmer's son is still in the white woman's power, his wife thinks up a plan. She dresses as a boy and lets the white woman chase her. In this way the white woman crosses the border of her territory and falls into the hands of a man who manages to drown her.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"BOEKV094","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"The son does not want to kill her because he wants her as his wife. For a year father and son never leave the girl alone, but after a year they have to go out together after all. The girl manages to escape. The son runs after her and throws an axe at her, but he misses. The girl tells the schout (sheriff) everything, and the two murderers are beheaded. At the spot where the two murdered so many people, the victims still haunt as witte wieven (white women).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0161"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"ENGELB_13_014","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man manages to get into the farmhouse; the Hun throws the axe after him, and it lands in the doorpost.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0161"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CBOEK305","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"If anyone disturbs her rest, she wrings his neck. A strong man goes to the castle she haunts at night and destroys her for good.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ005402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"In the Zwagerbosch he suddenly saw five women standing there wearing pointed caps and long white skirts. There was not a breath of wind, yet the plumes of the caps waved to and fro. He was frightened to death and went to old Bearn's farm. When they went to look together, the women were gone.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"VODA_035_14","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The old farmhand is afraid. A young, fearless farmhand offers to take the horses to the meadow and bring them back from now on. One day the young farmhand also sees a burning candle on the gate and two floating ladies. The horses are restless. The farmhand knocks the candle off the gate and the two ladies vanish at once. The horses are calm again. From then on, however, the young farmhand is tormented night after night by the white lady, who wants her light back, and after six weeks he dies of it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"TINNEV065","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The group starts running. When they have stopped running, the first man tells them he saw a grijze juffer (grey lady).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310F"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"LYST280","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Because he insults them, one of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0161"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"TINNEV038","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They dance until the man can go on no longer and drops dead.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ001413","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He murdered his aunt for her money and since then it has been haunted there. All this happens close to the spot where the house of strong Hearke once stood.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘girl’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0161. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"stack":["c1","c5"]},"found_card":{"card":"c5"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3541,"rank":1.004,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ112315","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot two white girls wander about. Such a witte juffer (white lady) is also said to have haunted another place.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/30078","original":"Op it Skier spoeken twa famkes, dy wienen hielendal yn 't wyt. Om ien ûre yn 'e nacht wienen se warber. In man hat se dêr sjoen, hy hat it my sels forteld.\nDer mat hjir ek in wite juffer spoeke ha.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ057202","role":"member","render":{"description":"Near Westergeest a witte juffrouw (white lady) always used to haunt.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25824","original":"Oan 'e Wâlddyk ûnder Westergeast, dy kant nei Beintema's hûs op spûke altyd in wite juffer.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEUNING003202","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man who mocks the devil is lifted up and flung back and forth.","place":"Jistrum","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130981","original":"K. wier in ûnminske. Hy sloech syn wiif, hy forsoepte syn lean en hy swetste en flokte, dat it hwat die. Op in joun let roun hy op de Tilleloane en rôp, dat hy boppe Eestrum roun fleane soe as de duvel. Ynienen waerd hy opnaem en in kear of hwat hinne en wer oer de loane smiten. Doe rôp hy, dat hy it nea wer dwaen soe.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ111314","role":"member","render":{"description":"You need not be afraid of witte juffers (white ladies) haunting about. The white ghost women can be driven away, the black ones cannot.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29719","original":"Men heart wolris fan wite juffers dy't spoekje. Dêr hoeft men net bang foar to wêzen. Wyt kin fordreaun wurde, mar swart net.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Jistrum belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0967,"rank":0.8305,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST075","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a wedding one of the guests remarks that they forgot to invite the witte wieven (white women). When someone mockingly calls out to the witte wieven, an axe is thrown at his head. He just manages to flee inside in time. The door still shows the marks of the axe. The witte wief (white woman) calls out that she could have caught him if she had not lost her little shoe.","place":"Zenderen","prov":"Ov.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"M.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13289","original":"Parallel met het verhaal van de \"spinvisite\" loopt ook 't verhaal van de \"brulfte\" (bruiloft) waar een van de gasten tegen de \"brulfteneugers\" opmerkt dat hij de \"nögste noabers\" n.l. de \"witte wieve\" heeft vergeten. De \"brulfteneuger\" laat dat niet op zich zitten, gaat naar buiten en nodigt \"de witte wieve\" uit, op spottende toon. Hij wordt onmiddelijk achterna gezeten, vlucht nog net binnenshuis, terwijl hem de bijl nagegooid wordt en 'n snee in de niendeure maakt die nog aan de kleinkinderen van het bruidspaar vertoond wordt. Hier hoort ook weer dezelfde klacht over 't schoentje bij, dat niet was vastgestrikt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEUNING012603","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Two white women are said to walk in the churchyard at night.","place":"Genum","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131651","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ018116","role":"card","render":{"description":"A wit wief (white woman) haunts a certain haunted spot.","place":"Sumar","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20270"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELS003101","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witches fly on a broomstick, witte wieven (white women) float on the rim of a sieve.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210747","original":"Witte wiever:\nVroeger werd ons soms verteld, dat de heksen op een bezemsteel door de lucht vlogen. Witte wiever zweefden echter op een zeefrand (de houten spaanrand van een meelzeef) door de lucht.\n\nVerslag 55, Omzetting uit de Ned. taal in dialect van Helden, van de verhalen, ... onder no. L291-31. Helden, 10-12-1969\nWie we nag zo’n aankomende mèèdjes wore, vertèlde me, dét heksen dor de loocht vlogen op ennen beesemsjteel. Me sjpraak aug van Witte wiever. Die vlogen op enne zeve-rank dor de loocht. (Spaanrand van meelzeef).","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"YPFOE070a","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a crossroads near Jistrum it was haunted at night. One evening, after a party, one of Durk Jaringa's sons passed that crossroads and saw a white figure floating just in front of him. He ran head over heels back to Jistrum. Later some others took him home past the crossroads, but there was no longer anything to be seen of the figure.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12146","original":"Wite juffers\nTe Jistrum, oan 'e noardkant, dêr krúst de Spoekloane de wei dy't fan Jistrum nei de Grinzerstrjitwei rint. Op dat krúspunt doogde it lang net. Dêr gong wol ris in wite gestalte dwers oer de wei, flak foar de minsken lâns. Ik wit noch wol, dat ien fan Durk Jaringa's jonges-se wennen oan 'e grutte strjitwei- de jûnes nei 'De Lindeboom' yn Jistrum west hie - sa hiet de jachtweide fan Jan van der Schors. It hie der tige gesellich west, hy hie in slokje dronke en om in oere of tsien, alven sette er op hûs yn. Hy kaam dêr op dy fjouwersprong en dêr gong dy wite gestalte flak foar him lâns. Hy waard sa kjel, dat hy stode hals oer de kop wer nei Justrum ta en dêr fûn er andergeloks noch lju yn 'e herberch. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ064107","role":"card","render":{"description":"Father and Evert Bergsma from Tike are catching polecats together on the Gariperheide near Tuijen. There are tall trees there, and then Evert sees two trees coming towards him. They go around them. They are two white women wearing large, wide white skirts.","place":"De Tike","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27201","original":"Heit en Evert Bergsma fan de Tike wienen us op in joun togearre oan 't murdejeijen. Sy wienen yn Gariperheide op 'e Tuijen. Dêr stienen hege beammen. Doe sei Evert ynienen: \"Hwat is dat dêr?\"\nDêr wienen twa, dy kommen op har ta.\n\"Wy matte dêr mar net lâns\", sei heit. Doe binne se dêr omhinne gien. 't Wienen twa wite froulju, dy hienen greate wide wite rokken oan.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Genum. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"window","text":"Genum"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c2","word":"two","stained":"c2"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":1.1309,"rank":0.9121,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL003","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand tells his girl that he has an errand to run, and that if she meets a vicious dog she must give it her handkerchief. She does indeed meet a dog, throws the handkerchief at it and flees. During the meal it is seen that he has pieces of a handkerchief between his teeth. When his room is searched, the belt that turns someone into a werewolf is found. As soon as the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who was working far away, is standing by the oven trying to jump into the fire. After the belt has burned, the farmhand is released.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1894,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9505","original":"De weerwolf\nEr was eens een boerenknecht die soms een weerwolf was.\nDe knecht vrijde met een van de meiden, maar zij wist van de prins geen kwaad. Op een keer waren ze een eind buiten het dorp gaan wandelen. Toen ze op huis aangingen, viel de schemer in.\nOpeens had de knecht zin weerwolf te worden.\nHij zei tegen de meid: \"Ik moet hier even een boodschap doen. Loop jij maar vast door, ik haal je wel in. Mocht je een kwade hond tegenkomen, die je wil bijten, gooi hem dan mijn zakdoek toe. Dan heeft hij iets om zijn tanden in te zetten, terwijl jij ervandoor gaat.\"\nHij ging weg, en een poosje later zag ze een grote hond op zich afkomen. Ze gooide hem de zakdoek toe en zette het op een lopen. Het dier scheurde de zakdoek aan flarden en at hem op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BOEKV179","role":"card","render":{"description":"A youth is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the youth's teeth. Werewolves always wear a band around their waist. The farmer the youth works for burns the band. The werewolf still tries to get into the fire, but he is held back. When the band has burned, the youth is an ordinary person again.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1896,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"G.J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35060","original":"Van een Weerwolf.\n\nOp de Achterste hoef woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op een eigenaardige manier zijn ze daar achter gekomen.\nDie knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buiten dorps (1) geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet meer zoo heel ver van huis toen voelde hij een onweerstaanbare lust om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte het natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens (2) van den weg af bij genen boer zijn; ga gij maar door: ik zal u wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die op u aan bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij misschien wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG185","role":"card","render":{"description":"A young man is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the young man's teeth. This is how they know he is a werewolf.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46940","original":"No. 185. Op de Achterste hoef bij Bladel woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op 'n vreemde manier zijn ze dat aan de weet gekomen. Die knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buitendorps geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker, toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet ver meer van huis toen hij een onweerstaanbaren lust voelde om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte dat natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens van den weg af bij genen boer zijn, ga gij maar door: ik zal oe wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die naar oe bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST009","role":"card","render":{"description":"A couple go for a walk in the evening. The boy has to relieve himself, but before he disappears into the bushes he advises the girl that if a beast attacks her, she should throw her handkerchief in front of its mouth. A dangerous beast does indeed come at the girl. She throws her handkerchief in front of its jaws and the beast tears it apart. When the boy comes back, the girl sees that he has remnants of her handkerchief between his teeth. She now knows he is a werewolf and tells him so. The boy disappears and never came back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13223","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen vrijer bracht 's avonds z'n meisje naar huis. Onderweg zei ie: \"Ik moet even mijn behoefte doen. Als je in tussentijd een dier of zoiets op je af ziet komen, gooi het dan je zakdoek voor z'n kop.\" Toen de jongen weg was, kwam er een dier op het meisje aangelopen. Ze slingerde haar zakdoek voor z'n muil en het beest verscheurde hem. Even later kwam de jongen terug en hij vroeg zijn meisje of er iets gebeurd was. Ze vertelde wat er was voorgevalllen en terwijl keek ze hem strak aan. Toen zei ze hem: \"Ik geloof, dat jij het beest bent geweest, want je hebt de stukken zakdoek nog tussen je tanden zitten\" Onmiddellijk was de vrijer verdwenen, en het meisje heeft hem nooit teruggezien.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with H. 12 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"471a2ca754b545a5","accepted_hashes":["253538a03c450255bff11c1f2c76afc9b4f5fb22b23b086c5c40dc211cb6e366","5a82b0a655ba58c8273be381da83c222a0c6e72bedd8112b92a074ee580a6ace","b92039814b443e7b25f7e0c510b0229449efa0985b8d96b1072814b007b3de74","fab1e14f32397f7cf0130c1d58faa735aee9964c628e10ba903068e0dcd37a34"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1214,"rank":0.543,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ115519","role":"member","render":{"description":"A werewolf is someone who is never full: he just keeps on eating. One of seven boys in a household is a werewolf.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1977,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/31124","original":"In wjerwolf is ien dy't net sêd kin. 't Kin neat skele hoefolle er hawn hat, hy kin altyd wol wèr ite. Ien út in húshâlding fan sawn jonges is in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ046513","role":"member","render":{"description":"Of seven boys born in succession, one is a werewolf or a devil-banisher.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24459","original":"Fan ien fan 'e sawn jonges, dêr't net in fanke tusken is, is ien in wearwolf of in duvelbanner.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ054504","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven boys born in succession is a werewolf. The narrator tells of a boy, one of seven sons, who is a werewolf and feels the urge to tear all sorts of things apart.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25484","original":"Ien fan sawn opelkoarfolgjende jonges is in wjerwolf.\nYn 'e Moedershoeke, hjir yn 'e Boelensloane wenne Brant Veenstra. Dy hie sawn jonges. Ien fan dy jonges is Hindrik. Dat wie in wjerwolf. Syn eigen heit sei: \"Hindrik is in raren, 't is in forskuorreling.\"\nOp in kear siet er op 't hûske. Syn broer Germ pleage him oan 'e bûtenkant. Doe fleach Hindrik sa fan 't hûske ôf mei de broeken by 't gat del op syn broer ta en seamde him ôf.\nHy ropte soms mei de tosken de bûsdoeken útelkoar.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ009726","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Witte wieven (white women) mostly haunt on wooden planks.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17542","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Harkema belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0596,"rank":0.5128,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST189","role":"card","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"EDJSL012","role":"card","render":{"description":"A day labourer is returning home and sees a plough with no horse or man coming towards him. The plough changes shape: it is the smallholder, standing before him. The smallholder begs the man not to give him away.\nAt haymaking time the two men work together. When the smallholder is asleep, a mole comes out of his neck. The smallholder vomits litres of blood. In the meadow the remains of a calf are found; only a few gnawed bones are left. The smallholder dies. The priest has to come before the coffin can be carried to the churchyard.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1980,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9514","original":"Mol, de weerwolf\nEen keuterboer, die Mol heette, werd altijd uitgescholden:\n\"Bierpoep! Twee emmers vol snijbonen en nog maar wind!\"\nDat kwam omdat hij zoveel at.\nKarels, een dagloner, keerde 's avonds laat dwars door het veld terug naar huis, toen hij een ploeg zonder paard of man op zich af zag komen. Hij trok zijn mes, maar het ketste af op het ploegijzer. De ploeg veranderde van gedaante, en in de man die voor hem stond, herkende hij Mol.\nDeze viel op zijn knieën en smeekte hem niet te verraden. Hij zou Karels een mud boekweit en een mud rogge geven.\n\"Van jou, weerwolf, wil ik geen boekweit of rogge,\" zei de boerenknecht. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ007505","role":"door","render":{"description":"In a family of seven boys, the eldest, youngest or middle one is a werewolf, a man who looks like a beast and must kill.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16994","original":"As der yn in húshâlding sawn jonges binne, is de âldste of de jongste of de middelste in wjerwolf. In wjerwolf, dat is in man, dy't de natuer hat fan in beest; ien dy't formoardzje mat.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6696,"rank":0.25,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV009505","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At midnight the ghost of a murdered person haunts and blood spatters up at the place of the murder. A boy then does not dare look over his right shoulder.","place":"Stadskanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44586"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV015701","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Late in the evening a man notices that the back door of the cowshed is open and hears rumbling that does not come from the cows. The farmer says that a woman who was murdered there haunts now and then.","place":"Musselkanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45797","original":"Mien voader kon kwoad zain en hef mie door veul van verteld. Hai dainde as jongkerel bie de boer. Op n keer kwam e wat loat in hoes. Dan gung e deur de achterdeure van de dele, umdat andere deurn dicht zatn. As hai dan dele opstapt, heurt hai n geluud, man zug niks. \n“Kou lös”, denkt e. Hai zöcht n schienvat op en gait de baistn bie langs. Man nee heur, alles is rustig. \n Zeker wat verbeeld, zo denkt hai. Nich laank loater overkomp hum t zulfde; weer gestommel op dele en t binnen gain koi-en, dai t doun. \nNon wait hai nich meer, wat e door van denkn mout. Wol wait hai wizze, dat e nooit meer deur de baanderdeure wil. \nAnder dag under t eetn proot hai dr over mit de boer. Dai zeg eerst niks. …","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ105507","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At night one can sometimes see the white apparition of a murdered woman.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37578","original":"Mem fortelde, hjir yn 'e Pein hat in huzinge stien mei in gracht der by. Dêr is alris in frommeske formoarde woarn. Sûnt seach men dêr nachts in frou yn 't wyt troch de gracht hinne rinnen. Dat wie dat formoarde frommeske.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Groningen a time of day was mentioned: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1965.","That card names a time of day. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"471a2ca754b545a5","accepted_hashes":["146360beefd172e26db004ea297031ad015fd82d2f5f2094c354363a63211be7","62d86881103315c15433ca480b1f2795c64dd557f9fe5d52e01f67ba256b87b2","7de2695c1bd5f33f07b9bf07ba4797ddb96eca4601a51027bf50fbef62c7176a","997899cf4f20026a294d5479710a008793e7d5adc94fccbaa5fd0b83016b3eba","ca76d932dabc3c9c2153605bcff09d60454ba6df96d78337e2a23abd77ff2337"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1065,"rank":0.515,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"SINBRABSAG078","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Aalst, a farmer's wife's daughter saw a spirit while she was milking the cow. She was very frightened and the next day the farmhand went with her. He saw the spirit too. The spirit came closer every evening, and the priest said they should ask the spirit what it desired. The farmer's wife, the farmhand and the daughter asked the spirit what it desired, and it told them it had vowed to make a pilgrimage to Kevelaar but had never fulfilled it. They decided to make the pilgrimage all together. After the journey the spirit was released and could go to heaven.","place":"Voldijn","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46713","original":"No. 78. Iederen avond ging de dochter van een boer uit Aalst met een paar meiden de koeien melken, tot zij op zekeren avond aan den rand van een bosch, op flinken afstand, een witte gedaante zag verschijnen. Ze werd bang en liep naar huis, zonder de koeien verder te melken. Ze kon niet spreken van angst en schrik, omdat ze niet wist wat 't was, en kwam hijgend van 't loopen thuis aan. De huisgenooten vroegen direct wat er aan de hand was, en toen zei ze, na tot bedaren gekomen te zijn, dat 't kon gaan zooals 't wilde, maar ze ging niet meer alleen melken, zoo was ze geschrokken. Den volgenden avond ging de knecht mee, omdat ze alleen niet meer wilde. Ze zagen dezelfde gedaante weer, maar nu kwam ze veel dichter bij. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"SINBRABSAG080","role":"member","render":{"description":"A poor broom-maker saw the spirit of his father, who had recently died, sitting on the wheelbarrow. His father told him he had to make a pilgrimage and give bread to the poor, because his father had made a vow that he had not kept. After these words his father disappeared.","place":"Eersel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46715","original":"No. 80. Omstreeks 1840 ging de arme bezembinder R. v. G. uit Eersel hei snijden. Nadat hij zijn vracht op de kruiwagen geladen had, rustte hij in de Zanddreef wat uit. Toen hij zijn tocht wilde voortzetten zat de geest van zijn vader, die voor kort gestorven was, op z'n kruiwagen. Hij beval zijn zoon om een beevaart te doen en den armen een brood te geven, want hij had tijdens zijn leven, een belofte niet nagekomen. Daarop verdween de geest, zonder een spoor achter te laten. 2)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG081","role":"member","render":{"description":"The spirit of the priest asks a pious person whether she will do a good work for him, so that he can enter heaven.","place":"Westerhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46716","original":"No. 81. Het gebeurde op het gehucht Loveren, anderen zeggen in het braambosch, onder Westerhoven. De pastoor was gestorven, en zijn geest verscheen aan een vroom kwezelken, en verzocht haar spoedig een goed werk voor hem te laten doen, dan zou hij zalig worden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ039817","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man asks his sweetheart for a handkerchief and disappears with it. When he returns, red threads from the handkerchief hang between his teeth. He confesses that he is a werewolf who must tear something apart now and then, and had asked for a handkerchief so as not to tear her apart.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23534","original":"Der wienen in feint en in faem, dy wienen togearre út to riden.\nUnderweis lei de feint de swipe del en hy liet it hynder stilstean.\nDe faem sei tsjin 'e feint: \"Hwat silstû?\"\n\"Jow my de bûsdoek\", sei er. Doe joech se him in reade bûsdoek. Dêr gong er mei fuort.\nDoe't er in skoftsje fuort west hie, kom er werom. Doe hied er de reade triedden fan 'e bûsdoek tusken de tosken hingjen.\n\"Hwat hastû dien?\" sei se.\nDoe hied er bikend dat er in wjerwolf wie. Hy moest nou en dan hwat forskuorre. Dêrom hied er om 'e bûsdoek frege, oars hied er har forskuorre matten.\nDoe hat dy faem de forkearing gau út makke.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Harkema belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1229,"rank":0.3333,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"VODA_002_16","role":"top","render":{"description":"A castle near Eersel is haunted. A brave man from the village goes to investigate. While waiting, he bakes pancakes over a fire.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1976,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69637","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VODA_002_16","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"Each time a pancake is done, a limb falls out of the chimney, until at midnight they form a skeleton that comes to life. The skeleton points him to the cellar, where there are three chests of gold. When the chests are divided between the man, the church and the poor, the ghost can rest.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"three"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ060811","role":"half","render":{"description":"Later, at this spot, a blue woollen apron hung over the hedge, which had appeared in place of the ghost. The hedge stands close to the Spookplaats.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0477"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST263","role":"half","render":{"description":"The legend goes that around midnight a white lady who used to live at the castle is seen haunting those woods.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ100109","role":"half","render":{"description":"The father saw nothing, but the dog ran home terrified. The boy then saw the apparition run into the fields, and never dared to go to that spot again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"BRUIJNZILV012","role":"half","render":{"description":"After thinking hard, he pictures having buried the pot of money under a willow. Mother and son go digging but find nothing. The neighbour girl's magic marble rolls away and comes to rest at the spot where the treasure is buried.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ019718","role":"half","render":{"description":"In the end flames even shoot out of the chest. It is said that the treasure chest will only stop sinking when a white billy goat runs over the spot.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘man’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c2","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c2"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1","word":"three","stained":"c2"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
